% The result model of precedential constraint (Horty), as a plain-LE library.
%
% Include it ("... includes these resources: precedent.") and supply, for each
% open-textured issue: rules naming its factors ("a damage has factor
% suddenness if the damage occurred suddenly"), which factors favour or
% disfavour it ("suddenness favours accidental"), and the case base: facts
% about each decided case, cited with provenance trailers ("kitchen flood has
% factor suddenness, as stated in decision D-1 at paragraph 4"; "kitchen flood
% decided for accidental, according to the ombudsman, ...").
%
% A situation is forced for an issue by a precedent that decided for it when
% the situation has at least the precedent's pro-factors and at most its
% con-factors (a fortiori); symmetrically against. See precedent_pattern.le.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    *a situation* has factor *a factor*.
    *a factor* favours *an issue*.
    *a factor* disfavours *an issue*.
    *a case* decided for *an issue*.
    *a case* decided against *an issue*.
    *a situation* is forced for *an issue* by *a case*.
    *a situation* is forced against *an issue* by *a case*.
    *an issue* has an inconsistent case base.

the knowledge base precedent includes:

a situation is forced for an issue by a case
    if the case decided for the issue
    and for all cases in which
            a factor favours the issue
            and the case has factor the factor
        it is the case that
            the situation has factor the factor
    and for all cases in which
            a second factor disfavours the issue
            and the situation has factor the second factor
        it is the case that
            the case has factor the second factor.

a situation is forced against an issue by a case
    if the case decided against the issue
    and for all cases in which
            a factor disfavours the issue
            and the case has factor the factor
        it is the case that
            the situation has factor the factor
    and for all cases in which
            a second factor favours the issue
            and the situation has factor the second factor
        it is the case that
            the case has factor the second factor.

% A case base is inconsistent when one of its decisions would be forced the
% other way by another.
an issue has an inconsistent case base
    if a first case decided for the issue
    and the first case is forced against the issue by a second case.

